  <layout>One printed page of verse in two stanza groups, set in one column; running head at top with page number at top right; no margin notes.</layout>
  <page_number>159</page_number>
  <running_head>ABRA. SACRIFICANS.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Abramus abfens audiit, ilicet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Vernas trecentos, bisque nouem simul</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Collegit, armis muniit, &amp; feros</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Sequutus hostes fortiter iruit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Et terga dantes funditus obruit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Potens supremi præsidio Patris.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Dehinc dura rupit vincula, &amp;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>aneas Vinctis catenas, &amp; decimis prius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Summo solutis Pontifici sua</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Turba miselle restituit bona,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Prædasque raptas. Sic rediit domum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Victor decorus, totaque totius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Orbis tremendo reddidit arbitro.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Quum tot niteret plena bonis domus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Gemmis &amp; auro, nec pareret suo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Prolem marito iam senior Sara,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Vltro ipsa seruam tradidit Abrahæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Si forte tali coniugio placens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Nascatur hares, cui sua linquerēt</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Post fata grandes diuitias pater.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Hac Ismaelem serua tulit ferum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Cui regna seclis post venientibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Promisit arcus sydereæ potens,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Censusque opimos, &amp; varium decus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Sacris sed ipsa ad mancipium adibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Exire iussit, legitimum ut viro</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printed text is partly damaged at the right edge of the stanzas; a few words are doubtful, e.g. "totaque totius" in line 6 of the second stanza, "sua" and "linquerēt" may be misread. The text continues past the bottom of the page.</notes>
</page>
